---
id: org.dxos.features
name: DXOS feature map
version: 0.1.0
---

The feature map is the top of the chain that turns intent into working code:
feature map > spec > review > tasks > code > result. Each `feature` states a goal and cites the spec
items that describe it; the format is `packages/reflect/deus/lang/features.mdl`.

- `pnpm deus features check` shows each feature's status beside the status its spec reviews support.
- To add or change a feature, edit its block here with a `## Changelog` decision, then carry it down
  the layers with the `feature-waterfall` skill (`agents/routines/feature-waterfall.md`).

The map was seeded with one feature per spec, its status taken from that spec's review. Split a
feature into narrower ones (citing `#F-n` items) as the work on it gets specific.

## Extensions

| Term       | URI                         |
| ---------- | --------------------------- |
| `feature`  | `org.dxos.mdl.feature@1.0`  |
| `decision` | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0` |

## Features

### Apps

```mdl
feature composer-app.app: Composer
  status: in-progress
  specs: [packages/apps/composer-app/spec/APP.mdl]
  note: Seeded from its review of 2026-10-27: 7 done, 3 partial, 1 diverged, 3 missing.
```

```mdl
feature composer-app.perf: Composer Performance
  status: operational
  specs: [packages/apps/composer-app/spec/PERF.mdl]
  note: Seeded from its review of 2026-10-27: 1 done.
```

