### New features

```mdl
feature plugin-zen.sleep-fade: Timed Dreams fade out instead of stopping
  status: operational
  specs: [packages/plugins/plugin-zen/PLUGIN.mdl#F-6]
  depends: [plugin-zen]
  note: |
    A timed Dream is for falling asleep, and an abrupt stop when the timer runs out wakes the listener.
    Over the last 30 seconds of a timed Dream (the whole Dream when it is shorter), the master volume
    ramps down to silence, then playback stops as it does today. Stopping by hand and untimed Dreams
    are unaffected.
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The feature map starts with one feature per reviewed spec, each marked with the status its review supports.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: The spec reviews of 2026-10-27 judged every spec in the repo, so a status derived from them is the most accurate starting point; per-spec features can be split later.
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Add plugin-zen.sleep-fade — a timed Dream fades its master volume to silence over its last 30 seconds before it stops.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  why: The first new feature to carry down the waterfall end to end; small, user-facing, and checkable by a unit test.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: plugin-zen.sleep-fade moves to in-progress.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [plugin-zen.sleep-fade]
  why: Its spec items now exist (PLUGIN.mdl F-6, commit a1525e46) and the review (commit 91bea605) finds the fade partly built; the remaining work is in the plugin-zen TASKS.md.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: plugin-zen.sleep-fade moves to operational.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [plugin-zen.sleep-fade]
  why: The code (commit 859c2f38) fades a timed Dream over its last 30 s, and the re-run review judges F-6.1, F-6.2 and F-6.3 done, each held by a unit test. It is marked operational ahead of its dependency plugin-zen, which stays in-progress: the fade does not rely on the untested parts of that spec.
  rejected:
    - Keep in-progress until plugin-zen is operational — the status would contradict the reviews of the items it cites.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: plugin-labeler is merged into plugin-inbox; its spec moves to plugin-inbox/docs/TRIAGE.mdl under the plugin-inbox feature, and the plugin-labeler feature is removed.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [plugin-inbox, plugin-labeler]
  why: Triage only ever acts on a mailbox, and as a separate opt-in plugin it was off wherever inbox was on.
```
